==Enemy==
This enemy appears in almost any level when the player takes too much time, normally when the player's [[Timed Score Reward|timed score]] reaches 0. She is not a threat and is mostly just there to signify that you are taking too long, however she still does attack, dealing one damage per hit. In some levels, there are different conditions for how and when Ms. Sign spawns, and in an even smaller selection of levels, they indicate [[Assassin Bear]]s that are about to be spawned:
*Specifically in [[Chubby B. Goode]], Ms. Sign spawns twice (first at 10 mins, second one at 14 mins, 26.67s), and after that the player will end up facing highly magnified Assassin Bears afterwards. This also happens in [[Murmuring Evil]], but with half as much time for the Ms. Signs to spawn.
*In [[Last Gang]], Ms. Sign spawns earlier than usual (126.67 seconds), along with a large horde of Assassin Bears.
*In both [[Star Ocean]] and [[Celestial Seas]], Ms. Sign spawns at 200 seconds to indicate a swarm of massively buffed [[Doge Dark]]s and [[Gabriel]]s spawning respectively.
*The Ms. Sign in [[Kugel Schreiber]] spawns as a boss after 233.33 seconds. Killing her will result in an Assassin Bear spawning.
*Strangely, in [[Learned to Love]], Ms. Signs are completely replaced by Assassin Bears.

==Strategy==
You can use almost any unit to beat Ms. Sign, as her attack power is laughably low, and her health goes down very quickly, despite it being above most other [[:Category:Empire of Cats Enemies|Empire of Cats Enemies]].

There is a "cheesing strategy" for many levels (notably [[Dark Souls (Insane)|Dark Souls]] and [[Deathhawk (Deadly)|Deathhawk]]) with weak to mid-level peons involving Ms. Sign. Normally, it exploits her ten thousand knockbacks. If you wait for Ms. Signs to stack up until the enemy limit is reached (10 in the aforementioned stages), no other enemies will spawn, including the boss. From there you can use [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cats]] to knock her back, and then summon your high-damage attackers. Note that this takes '''75 minutes WITH A [[Speed Up|SPEED UP]],''' so it should only be used as a last resort.

