==Trivia==
*Her Japanese name has a double meaning: while ''Kanban Musume'' literally translates to "Signboard Girl", it can also refer to an attractive girl who stands outside a store to attract customers.
**This may be why her description in the original [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|Battle Cats]] said, "She is a slut."
*Prior to version 1.5.2, the sign message changed depending on the device language (English or Japanese). However, after version 2.0.0, the [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|original English version]] was lost. The English text used to be "Too late!! Come back stronger!!".
**In the [[The Battle Cats|English re-release]], her sign reads "<font color="red">Too slow!!</font> Try harder next time!!".
*In the Korean version, [[Doge]] is listed as part of her family structure instead of a "daddy".
*She has the second-highest amount of knockbacks in the game, with [[Gummy Cat (Enemy)|Gummy Cat]] in the first place.
*Ms. Sign is the only enemy in the game which does not appear when viewing the enemies in a stage.
*She does not appear in most stages with a [[Stage Difficulties|difficulty]] of ★10 or more, possibly because of the infamous cheesing strategy. This includes all [[Uncanny Legends]] stages except for [[An Ancient Curse]], [[Murmuring Evil]], [[Furry Cavern]], [[Hall of the Four Kings]], [[Aku Altar's Seal]] and [[Night of the Hustler]].
*In [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou]], her role was overtaken by [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Kemedama|Kemedama]] holding a sign with the same message.
*In the Spanish, French and German translations of the game, the text on her sign is still in English.
*Some of the possible [[Cat Shrine#Cat Fortune|Cat Fortunes]] are "Ms. Sign will destroy your [[Cat Base]]." and "Ms. Sign will soon get tired of waiting..."

